{"id":"h22t3","name":"Weekly Leaderboard Movers","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>scores</b> has the columns <code>player</code>, <code>played_on</code> (date) and <code>points</code>. A week starts on Monday (<code>date_trunc('week', played_on)</code>, as a date). The weekly score of a player is the sum of their points in that week.</p>\n<p>Each week, players are ranked by weekly score with <code>DENSE_RANK</code> (highest score = rank 1, equal scores share a rank). Only players with at least one row in the week are ranked that week.</p>\n<p>The leaderboard of a week shows the players with a rank from 1 to 3 (so it can show more than 3 players). For each of them, <code>move</code> compares with the <b>calendar week just before</b>: <code>'NEW'</code> if the player was not ranked that week, <code>'='</code> if the rank is the same, else the number of places gained with a sign, like <code>'+2'</code> (better rank) or <code>'-1'</code> (worse rank).</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the columns <code>week</code>, <code>rnk</code>, <code>player</code>, <code>score</code> and <code>move</code>, sorted by <code>week</code>, then <code>rnk</code>, then <code>player</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>scores</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>player</th><th>played_on</th><th>points</th></tr><tr><td>ana</td><td>2026-03-02</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>ana</td><td>2026-03-04</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>ben</td><td>2026-03-03</td><td>60</td></tr><tr><td>cyd</td><td>2026-03-05</td><td>40</td></tr><tr><td>dan</td><td>2026-03-06</td><td>30</td></tr><tr><td>eve</td><td>2026-03-08</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>ana</td><td>2026-03-09</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>ben</td><td>2026-03-10</td><td>70</td></tr><tr><td>cyd</td><td>2026-03-11</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>dan</td><td>2026-03-12</td><td>70</td></tr><tr><td>fay</td><td>2026-03-15</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>ana</td><td>2026-03-23</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>fay</td><td>2026-03-24</td><td>5</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>week</th><th>rnk</th><th>player</th><th>score</th><th>move</th></tr><tr><td>2026-03-02</td><td>1</td><td>ana</td><td>60</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-02</td><td>1</td><td>ben</td><td>60</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-02</td><td>2</td><td>cyd</td><td>40</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-02</td><td>3</td><td>dan</td><td>30</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-09</td><td>1</td><td>cyd</td><td>90</td><td>+1</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-09</td><td>2</td><td>ben</td><td>70</td><td>-1</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-09</td><td>2</td><td>dan</td><td>70</td><td>+1</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-09</td><td>3</td><td>ana</td><td>20</td><td>-2</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-09</td><td>3</td><td>fay</td><td>20</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-23</td><td>1</td><td>ana</td><td>5</td><td>NEW</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-23</td><td>1</td><td>fay</td><td>5</td><td>NEW</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>scores</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>week</code>, <code>rnk</code>, <code>player</code>, <code>score</code>, <code>move</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["DENSE_RANK","égalités","comparaison semaine précédente","texte calculé (+2, -1, =, NEW)","top N avec ex aequo"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>scores</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 5 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>week</code>, <code>rnk</code>, <code>player</code>, <code>score</code>, <code>move</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"scores":{"columns":[["player","TEXT"],["played_on","DATE"],["points","INT"]],"rows":[["ana","2026-03-02",50],["ana","2026-03-04",10],["ben","2026-03-03",60],["cyd","2026-03-05",40],["dan","2026-03-06",30],["eve","2026-03-08",20],["ana","2026-03-09",20],["ben","2026-03-10",70],["cyd","2026-03-11",90],["dan","2026-03-12",70],["fay","2026-03-15",20],["ana","2026-03-23",5],["fay","2026-03-24",5]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["week","rnk","player","score","move"],"rows":[["2026-03-02",1,"ana",60,"NEW"],["2026-03-02",1,"ben",60,"NEW"],["2026-03-02",2,"cyd",40,"NEW"],["2026-03-02",3,"dan",30,"NEW"],["2026-03-09",1,"cyd",90,"+1"],["2026-03-09",2,"ben",70,"-1"],["2026-03-09",2,"dan",70,"+1"],["2026-03-09",3,"ana",20,"-2"],["2026-03-09",3,"fay",20,"NEW"],["2026-03-23",1,"ana",5,"NEW"],["2026-03-23",1,"fay",5,"NEW"]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"scores":{"columns":[["player","TEXT"],["played_on","DATE"],["points","INT"]],"rows":[["x","2026-01-05",1],["y","2026-01-05",1],["z","2026-01-06",0],["w","2026-01-07",-3],["w","2026-01-12",9],["x","2026-01-13",1],["z","2026-01-14",1]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["week","rnk","player","score","move"],"rows":[["2026-01-05",1,"x",1,"NEW"],["2026-01-05",1,"y",1,"NEW"],["2026-01-05",2,"z",0,"NEW"],["2026-01-05",3,"w",-3,"NEW"],["2026-01-12",1,"w",9,"+2"],["2026-01-12",2,"x",1,"-1"],["2026-01-12",2,"z",1,"="]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}